      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our circle is centered at $(\\frac{3}{2},- \\frac{5}{2})$ and has a radius of $\\frac{7}{2},$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y-\\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right))^{2}={\\frac{7}{2}}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{49}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{49}{4}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-\\frac{3}{2})^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x-\\frac{3}{2})+2(y+\\frac{5}{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+\\frac{5}{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x-\\frac{3}{2}}{y+\\frac{5}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
